[Music]  hello and welcome to PlayStation granade  how would you raise your abilities as a  competitive game  I've always classed myself as mediocre  the most average player in the lobby  my aim is substandard my reactions  distinctly average but I want to be good  at apex legends so I've been fine-tuning  the settings on console and I'm  delighted to say I found seven subtle  changes which will bridge the gap to the  pros and let even the most casual of  players compete for victory without  putting thirty hours a week in here's an  example when transitioning into apex  legends the old me could get the job  done but it was a train wreck of over  adjustment when aiming but now with my  updated settings my aim is reliable from  the first shot and stays on target far  easier so at last I'm not the weakest  player in the squad as our  let's start with sensitivity because  most of us just want to know what each  other is playing on what sensitivity  does everyone use initially I was  tempted to use a high sense due to  playing fortnight for the last year but  we need to get that mentality out of our  head quickly apex Legends rewards  consistent accuracy and although some  players will prosper at high cents the  majority will not small adjustments are  king here my suggestion is to up the  default sensitivity slightly to number 4  named high we are doing this for two  reasons  firstly this will give you enough speed  to dodge enemy fire and make yourself a  harder target to hit overall generally  increasing maneuverability but the  second reason is to retain control of  the ping system  this is our lifeline to teammates no pun  intended this is a team shooter for a  reason and sacrificing precision for  speed isn't the right thing to do  especially with such a prolonged time to  kill today  ex legends so we have our general sense  sorted but history shows us a slightly  slower aiming-down-sights sensitivity is  required to keep our shots on target in  your settings keep the ad S as default  which is number three because we've  already moved the general sensitivity up  this will automatically feel slower when  aiming down sights making mid-range to  long-range bites easier to keep enemies  in your reticle here's something I still  need to work on in close-up scenarios  try to use hipfire to maintain the speed  I'm still working on this but my muscle  memory forces me to aim before every  shot but one day I will get there and  I'm sure you'll master it before I do  the next step is surprisingly important  under AD s we have a response curve I  didn't really have a clue what this  meant so I tested things out for a while  the classic setting mirrors tighten  fault whose aiming or if you didn't play  that game it feels like how Modern  Warfare felt back in 2007 what happens  is as you move the reticle there is a  slight moment before the input it's  probably accepted by the console so  basically it's slowed down for a split  second whilst you start to move this is  primarily here to make tiny adjustments  in gunfights but secondly when done  correctly it feels like the weapon has  legitimate weight to it this is how the  human body actually works let's say  you're picking something off a table but  it's heavy for a millisecond while your  muscles figure out how much energy to  assert you pick up that item slower as  soon as your brain understands the  weight of the object you once again move  at top speed this is how response curves  work in video games on the other side of  the spectrum is linear and this setting  has no response curve at all the exact  movement of your thumb on the controller  happens in the game  those people with unbelievable quick  reactions who can play at high speed  will use this or a slightly easier  version called high velocity which now  brings us to the one I suggest steady  this is perfection in my eyes acting the  same as classic setting a steady aim  adds a little more of a ramp up to full  speed making two tiny adjustments at  long medium range even easier but when  it comes to throwing down ridiculous  amounts of bullets the steady curve  acceleration kicks in at the same time  as the weapon begins to recoil giving  you the ability to control the weapon  direction in addition to those tiny  adjustments weapons legitimately feel  heavier in this mode more lifelike  rather than like nerf guns please give  it a try I would love to know your  thoughts the next setting is dead zone  the best way to understand this is by  holding out your thumb now try to keep  it as still as you can however much you  try your hand will slightly move it's  impossible our heartbeat means that we  are always moving dead zones on  controllers are here in part to ignore  small movements in our thumbs another  reason why dead zones are important  comes down to wear and tear in your  controller over time your thumb sticks  will begin to lean to one side causing  your character to slowly walk in that  die  you have a few choices in this scenario  fix your controller buy a new one or  change the dead zone settings to tell  the console to ignore that imperfection  long story shot use small dead zones as  default or even none if you have a  controller under 18 months old and of  course have full control over your  thumbs unlike me  oh wait while we're here turn off  vibration yeah it's great and all but it  disrupts your control and disaffection  completely it'll also stop you saying ow  when someone shoots you in-game why do  we do that the next setting is another  game changer PC players have had this  for years but only a handful of console  games have this option field of view in  the video settings it's possible to  change your perspective from 70 degrees  to a whopping 110 degrees just look at  this difference look how much more you  can see on either side I have mine set  between 90 and 100 depending on how far  I sit from the screen and it's important  to know why here's an example it may  appear that maxing out this setting will  be the best option as you can see much  more of the battlefield but it  completely depends on what engagements  you're planning for and if you're  playing sat on a couch 2 meters away  from a 50-inch TV or sat at a desk with  a 24-inch monitor in front of your eyes  let's quickly break that down look at  the target in the distance at 70 degrees  of vision it's easy to track and rather  large target to aim for here's the same  thing at 110 degrees a much smaller  target and if you're sat far away from  the screen this is simply impossible to  hit I personally recommend between 90  and 100 for players playing close to the  screen or 70 to 80 for those in their  front room sat a meter or two away from  the action  oh there's another great thing about  widening the viewpoint it's feel the  entire game feels quicker you feel  superhuman ultra responsive just  remember not to overdo it or you'll be  useless to your team at range let's  quickly talk about button remapping and  that slide function without a doubt is a  beast which you'll use in and out of  battle I recommend anyone using a  standard controller to switch to the  setting button puncher this will remap  the melee and Crouch slide buttons  meaning that right thumbstick becomes  Crouch when pressed allowing you to keep  both thumb's on the sticks more often if  you have a pro controller or play cloth  it's regardless but for us mortals  button puncher is awesome let's quickly  look at audio or would it be listen to  audio just jump into audio settings if  you want to be competitive audio is key  so if you're playing without a headset  you're at a major disadvantage you are  not hearing the three-dimensional sound  but if you do have a headset you can  adjust things to get a little extra edge  although the music in apex is great it's  it's hugely distracting and can hide  'important audio queues I recommend  either lowering those settings are  completely switching them off the sound  of gunfire will quickly become the music  to your ears make sure your sound  effects are at full whack and depending  on your preference it's a good idea to  lower the dialogue option but I won't do  that because I love to hear this guy  spamming 12 grenades in a row  show my comrades look joke so there we  have it seven settings to make an  average APEC Legends player compete  against those people who have no life  I mean compete against those people who  wanted the pros I do hope this was  helpful in some way I am Adam from  Playstation grenade it's been a pleasure  I'll see you next time

